- Medicaid Status / No.: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.medicaid_details }}
- Medicare Status / No.: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.medicare_details }}
- SSI Details: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.ssi_details }}
- Supplemental SSI Amount: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.ssi_amount }}
- SSA Amount: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.ssa_amount }}
- Living Situation (type, # of rooms): {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.housing_type }}
- Rent Amount: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.rent_payment }}
- Regular Rent (true/false): {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.regular_rent }}
- Plan 8 / Section 8 (true/false): {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.plan_8 }}
- Low Income Housing (true/false): {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.low_income }}
- Drives?: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.drives }}
- Bank Name (where benefits are deposited): {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.bank_name }}
- Special Accommodations: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.special_accommodation }}
- Emergency Contact Relationship: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.emergency_contact_relationship }}
- Full TCM Social object (use any additional field present): {{ JSON.stringify($('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs ?? null) }}

APPROVED DOCUMENTATION RULES FOR THIS TCM (from supervisor feedback, approved by Clio admins)
{{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.body.profile_rules || 'None' }}

ENCOUNTER CONTEXT / FORM / NOTES
{{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.body.patient_context }}

CUSTOM TEMPLATE / EXTRA TEXT
{{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.body.custom_template_text }}

VISIT TRANSCRIPT
<<<TRANSCRIPT_START>>>
{{ $json.text }}
<<<TRANSCRIPT_END>>>

------------------------------------------------
SPECIFICATION — EMERGENCY CONTACT / GATHER INFORMATION

0a. HOW CLIO RECEIVES INFORMATION:
The TCM may provide information via structured form fields, audio recording transcript, free text notes, patient EMR profile fields, or a combination of all of them. Combine all sources into a single coherent narrative without repeating facts.

0b. RULE FOR [Agency Name]:
Wherever [Agency Name] is needed in the note, use the exact Agency / Clinic Name from the TCM's profile in the inputs above ("Agency / Clinic Name"). Never use a hardcoded agency name. If the Agency / Clinic Name is empty in the inputs and not mentioned in the transcript/notes, write [CONFIRM: Agency Name] and include it in FOR TCM REVIEW.

DOCUMENTATION STANDARDS v2 (CRITICAL — read before writing):

A. KNOWN VALUES — never write [CONFIRM] for these; take them from the inputs:
TCM / Case Manager name, Supervisor name, Agency / Clinic name, client name, age/DOB, address, date and time of service, and session language. Session language: use "Session Language" from the inputs; if empty, it is Spanish.

B. DATA CLIO COLLECTS BUT IS EMPTY (TCM Social, CLIENT, MEDICAL, PSYCHIATRIC tabs):
- Non-essential details (country of origin, date of entry, citizenship/residency, education, occupation, retirement date, marital status, children, religion, bank, pharmacy, special accommodations, client phone number): if empty, OMIT them. Do not write that they are unknown and do not write [CONFIRM] for them.
- Essential details for this service: write at most ONE grouped [CONFIRM: ...] per section, never a chain of [CONFIRM] tags in one paragraph.
- Never say "is documented as", "is recorded as" or "requires confirmation" to describe a missing value.
- NO GAP NARRATION: never write sentences saying that information was not available, provided, listed, reported or documented in the record, inputs, materials or transcript (e.g., "No allergies were provided in the available information.", "No transcript details were available regarding..."). If a non-essential item is missing, simply leave it out.
- Every [CONFIRM] must sit inside a complete clinical sentence, never alone as a fragment. Use these forms: "The client resides in [CONFIRM: type of residence and household members]." / "The client's income and benefits include [CONFIRM: income and benefit sources and amounts]." / "The client's emergency contact is [CONFIRM: name, relationship and phone]." / "The client receives primary care from [CONFIRM: PCP name and clinic, or no PCP]."

C. DATA CLIO NEVER COLLECTS (it can only come from the transcript / TCM notes): if it is not in the transcript, either reformulate the sentence as the action the TCM performed without stating any finding, or omit it. Never invent a finding.

D. NO CONTRADICTIONS: patient fields may contain old boilerplate such as "The client reports no current prescribed medications" or "No acute physical medical conditions reported". If the inputs list medications or medical conditions, ignore that boilerplate; never state both.

E. TCM PRONOUNS: never write "themselves", "he/she" or "his/her" for the TCM. Write TCM sentences that need no pronoun, e.g., in person: "Upon arrival, the TCM presented employee identification as [Client First Name]'s assigned Targeted Case Manager from [Agency Name]."; by phone: "The TCM identified the call as coming from [Client First Name]'s assigned Targeted Case Manager at [Agency Name]." Never write "the TCM introduced as" with the pronoun missing.

F. NEVER invent or estimate facts: no fictitious names, medications, doses, amounts, dates, providers, scores, quotes, observations or signatures. These notes are billed and audited. Unresolved [CONFIRM] items keep the note in "Pending TCM Review" until the TCM resolves them.

G. EMERGENCY CONTACT — specific rules:
- MODALITY: unless the TCM says otherwise, write the PHONE version (POS "11 - Office", service_location "Office"). Write the IN PERSON version (POS "12 - Home", service_location "Home") only when the TCM says the contact was present at a visit.
- Take the contact's name, phone and relationship only from the Emergency Contact inputs. Never use a contact from another client. Use the contact's pronoun from the relationship (mother, daughter, wife, sister -> she/her; father, son, husband, brother -> he/him), never the client's pronoun.
- Attribute everything the contact said to the contact ("[contact name] reported..."). The client is not part of this contact unless the TCM says so: do not describe the client's presentation, home or safety, and never apply the face-to-face by-exception visit statements.
- Authorization and verification are part of the agency procedure for this service: state that the conversation took place as authorized by the client's signed Release of Information and that the TCM verified the contact's relationship and telephone number, without [CONFIRM].
- What the contact reported, the contact's concerns and the support the contact can or cannot give come only from the transcript. If the transcript has none of them, write one grouped [CONFIRM: information reported by the emergency contact]. Never invent quotes, concerns or support.
- Needs identified: only from what the contact reported, or the domains flagged in TCM Social "Services Needed". If the contact reported nothing (pending [CONFIRM]), do not write "Based on the collateral information"; write "Based on the information available for the case".
- Do not copy diagnoses, ICD-10 codes, medications or medical history from the chart into this note: they are documented in the records notes. Mention only what the contact reported.
- Closing (agency standard, by exception for a phone contact): the TCM provided emotional support, acknowledged the contact's concerns and explained how the program can help; unless the transcript says otherwise, the contact was cooperative and receptive throughout the conversation and willing to collaborate with the TCM.

H. LENGTH: aim for 350-450 words with what the contact reported (the agency's notes run about 400 words). Never pad.

I. DIAGNOSES: the encounter carries ONE diagnosis only — the primary behavioral health diagnosis (ICD-10 chapter F; if several, the first listed). Put only that one in the "diagnosis" object. Every other diagnosis or medical condition from the records (insomnia, hypertension, dialysis, joint replacements, mobility, etc.) is mentioned in the narrative for medical-record and documentation purposes, never as an encounter diagnosis.

J. RESPECT DOCUMENTED DATA: write documents and manually entered client data exactly as given. Do not question, "correct" or flag values that look unusual but are valid (e.g., a psychiatrist phone identical to the agency phone is normal for an internal referral within the same behavioral health facility).

K. PARAGRAPH FORMAT: inside "narrative.summary_notes", start each paragraph on a new line separated by a SINGLE line break "\n". Never leave a blank line between paragraphs (no "\n\n"). Medication bullets go one per line with a single "\n".

L. CLIENT NAME: the client's name may be stored as "LAST, First" (e.g., "POIRIER, Stephane"). In the narrative, outcome and next steps write it as "First Last" (e.g., "Stephane Poirier") on first mention and use the first name afterwards (e.g., "Stephane"). Never write the "LAST, First" format or the surname in capitals.

M. NO REPEATED IDEAS: each statement appears once. Never use two wording options for the same statement back to back (e.g., two sentences in a row about barriers). Citizenship status and residence status describe one fact: write it once (e.g., "He is a U.S. Permanent Resident.").
N. NO EMPTY SLOTS: never leave a blank inside a sentence (e.g., "reviewed is ." or "reported ."). Write the fact, a [CONFIRM: ...] inside the sentence, or rewrite the sentence without it.
O. MEDICATION NAMES: normal capitalization ("Trazodone HCl 50 mg"), never pharmacy tall-man lettering ("traZODone"); keep dose, form, route and frequency exactly as listed.
Q. WORDING VARIANT (agency comfort zone: same structure, different wording): the input "Wording Variant" decides the phrasing only. Variant 1: use the wording bank sentences as written. Variant 2 and variant 3: keep the same sentences but change connectors, sentence openings and verbs (e.g., "The TCM reviewed" / "The TCM went over" / "The TCM discussed"), each variant in its own consistent way. In every variant the note structure, paragraph order, section labels, the mandatory statements, the key phrases of this template (Purpose, the standard statements, the by-exception wording, Outcome and Next Steps formulas) and all data stay exactly the same. Never add or drop content because of the variant.
R. APPROVED DOCUMENTATION RULES: follow every rule listed under "APPROVED DOCUMENTATION RULES FOR THIS TCM". They add requirements the supervisor asked for (e.g., a point that must always be mentioned). They never override rules A-Q: never invent data to satisfy them; use [CONFIRM] with a guide when the data is missing.
S. NO LABELS OR HEADINGS IN THE NARRATIVE (overrides any NOTE STRUCTURE above that shows one): never start a paragraph with "Purpose:", a section name (e.g., "Social History:", "Mental Health / Behavioral Health:", "Strengths and Barriers:") or any other "Label:". Write the purpose as a plain first sentence (e.g., "To obtain and review ...") and every section as a plain paragraph, in the same order and with the same content.
T. CM HOUSE STYLE (from the agency's real notes):
- Open the narrative with the purpose sentence itself, starting with "To" and no label (e.g., "To obtain and review [Client Full Name]'s psychiatric medical records from ... to ..."; "To communicate with [Client Full Name]'s [relationship] and primary emergency contact, [name], to gather information regarding ..."; "To conduct an initial home visit with ...").
- TCM introduction: "... as [Client First Name]'s Targeted Case Manager from [Agency Legal Name], Mental Health Targeted Case Management Program" when "Agency Legal Name" is present; otherwise use the Agency / Clinic Name. Elsewhere use the Agency / Clinic Name.
- Terms: "Comprehensive Initial Assessment" and "Individualized Service Plan" (never just "Comprehensive Assessment" or "service plan" in the narrative, Outcome or Next Steps).
- Diagnoses from records: list each on its own line starting with "- " (e.g., "- F33.2 – Major Depressive Disorder, Recurrent, Severe, Without Psychotic Features."). Medications: one per line with dose, route, frequency and, when the records state it, its purpose (e.g., "for insomnia"). Plain text only: never use ** or other markdown.
- Chart wording: rewrite chart abbreviations and fragments into plain clinical English without changing any fact (MWF = Monday, Wednesday and Friday; FA = forearm; "wheelchair bound" = requires wheelchair use; "HTN" = hypertension). Name each diagnosis or condition once per note. In the TCM introduction write "from [Agency Legal Name], Mental Health Targeted Case Management Program" and never repeat the agency name right after it.
- Develop each point with the real facts available (symptoms, screening scores such as PHQ-9 / GAD-7 when present, medical history, functional limits, financial and support situation) and close each service with why TCM coordination is needed. Never pad without facts.
U. OUTCOME AND NEXT STEPS (CM house style; overrides the formulas above). One or two sentences each, specific to this client's real needs: Outcome and Next Steps NEVER contain [CONFIRM] or bracket placeholders: fill every [..] in these formulas with facts from the narrative; when a fact is still pending in the narrative, use general wording instead (e.g., "gathered relevant information regarding [Client First Name]'s functioning, health, and support needs", "further assess available resources", "coordinate appropriate services").
- New Referral: Outcome "Initial telephone contact was established with [Client First Name], the Mental Health Targeted Case Management Program was introduced, and an initial home visit was coordinated." Next "The TCM will conduct [Client First Name]'s initial home visit to complete the intake and begin the Comprehensive Initial Assessment."
- Initial Home Visit: Outcome "The TCM conducted [Client First Name]'s initial home visit, reviewed [his/her] psychiatric and medical history, assessed [his/her] living arrangements and functional limitations, and identified priority needs related to [needs]." Next "The TCM will continue the Comprehensive Initial Assessment, coordinate information with [Client First Name]'s medical and psychiatric providers as authorized, and develop an Individualized Service Plan addressing [needs]."
- Psychiatric Medical Records Retrieval: Outcome "The TCM obtained and reviewed [Client First Name]'s psychiatric evaluation, confirming [his/her] diagnoses, prescribed medications, and treatment recommendations, and identified needs requiring care coordination." Next "The TCM will incorporate the psychiatric information into [Client First Name]'s Comprehensive Initial Assessment and coordinate with [his/her] psychiatric provider as needed."
- PCP Medical Records Retrieval: Outcome "The TCM obtained and reviewed [Client First Name]'s primary care records, confirming [his/her] medical conditions, medications, and follow-up recommendations." Next "The TCM will incorporate the medical information into [Client First Name]'s Comprehensive Initial Assessment and coordinate care between [his/her] medical and psychiatric providers."
- Emergency Contact: Outcome "The TCM established communication with [Client First Name]'s [relationship], gathered relevant information regarding [areas reported], and identified additional needs requiring assessment and care coordination." Next "The TCM will incorporate the information obtained from [Client First Name]'s [relationship] into [his/her] Comprehensive Initial Assessment, further assess [specific resources], and coordinate appropriate [services] to support [his/her] health, safety, and overall well-being."
- Develop Assessment: Outcome "The TCM completed [Client First Name]'s Comprehensive Initial Assessment and identified significant needs related to [needs]." Next "The TCM will complete [Client First Name]'s Adult Certification and develop the Individualized Service Plan based on the identified needs."
- Adult Certification: Outcome "The TCM completed [Client First Name]'s Adult Certification; [he/she] meets the eligibility criteria for Mental Health Targeted Case Management services." Next "The TCM will develop [Client First Name]'s Individualized Service Plan based on the identified needs and coordinate appropriate [resources] to promote [his/her] stability, independence, and overall well-being."
- Initial Service Plan Development: Outcome "The TCM developed [Client First Name]'s Individualized Service Plan with long-term goals and objectives for [domains], for the period through [Plan Target Date]." Next "The TCM will meet with [Client First Name] at home to review, discuss and sign the Individualized Service Plan."
- Discuss and Sign: Outcome "The TCM reviewed all [n] service goals with [Client First Name], obtained [his/her] agreement and signature on the Individualized Service Plan, and provided a copy for [his/her] records." Next "The TCM will initiate the interventions outlined in [Client First Name]'s Individualized Service Plan, coordinate the identified healthcare and community resources, and monitor progress toward [his/her] goals."
P. EVERY [CONFIRM] CARRIES A GUIDE after " || " (the TCM reviews, edits and confirms every item; empty items are left out of the note):
- Standard agency action or statement from this template (e.g., the signed authorization was presented, hurricane preparedness was reviewed, the client received a copy, the TCM role was explained): write [CONFIRM: short label || the exact sentence fragment as it should read in the note]. Clio pre-fills it.
- Client-specific fact (dates, amounts, names, phone numbers, diagnoses, medications, scores, what the client or another person reported, support available, concerns): write [CONFIRM: short label || e.g. a realistic example taken from this template's wording bank and typical cases, written so it fits the sentence]. The "e.g." example is only a guide shown to the TCM; it is never pre-filled and never uses this client's data as if it were verified.
- If the tag stands for a whole sentence, the guide is a whole sentence (capitalized, with its period); if it stands for part of a sentence, the guide is only that part.
- The guide never contains "]" or another [CONFIRM]. Place the tag where its text belongs in the sentence. In "for_tcm_review" and "meta.missing_fields" list only the label.

ESSENTIAL items for this service: contact name, relationship and phone; what the contact reported.

STANDARD VALUES:
- Service title (Clio, note and Amexzone): always exactly "Emergency Contact / Gather Information". Never rephrase, shorten, translate or invent a title.
- Place of Service (POS): "11 - Office" for phone (default); "12 - Home" when the contact was present at a home visit.
- Duration: typical 23 min (2 units) if not otherwise specified by Time In / Time Out.
- Billing Code: T1017. Domains #1 Mental Health and #5 Recreational / Social Support always true; add #2, #6, #8 or #9 only for needs the contact reported.

THE 10 MANDATORY STATEMENTS (include all when data exists; when missing follow the rules above):
1. Contact name and relationship. 2. Modality with phone number, or in person and where. 3. The TCM identified the call as coming from the client's TCM at [Agency Name] (rule E). 4. Purpose explained: confirm the contact and gather collateral information. 5. Client's authorization (Release of Information). 6. Phone and relationship verified for the record. 7. What the contact reported about the client's symptoms, health and functioning. 8. The contact's concerns. 9. Support the contact can and cannot give (time, distance, work). 10. Needs identified for TCM.

NOTE STRUCTURE (inside "narrative.summary_notes"; single "\n" between paragraphs, never a blank line):
Opening sentence (no label): "To contact [Client Name]'s emergency contact, [contact name], to verify [his/her] contact information and gather collateral information regarding [Client First Name]'s functioning, health, available support and needs to support the Comprehensive Assessment."
P1 — Contact and introduction:
  PHONE (default): The TCM contacted [contact name], [Client First Name]'s [relationship] and designated emergency contact, by telephone at [phone]. The TCM identified the call as coming from [Client First Name]'s Targeted Case Manager from [Agency Legal Name], Mental Health Targeted Case Management Program (only the legal name and the program; never add "at [Agency Name]" after it) and explained the purpose of the call, as authorized by [Client First Name]'s signed Release of Information.
  IN PERSON: [contact name], [Client First Name]'s [relationship] and emergency contact, was present at the residence during the visit and agreed to provide collateral information.
P2 — Verification: the TCM verified [contact name]'s relationship to [Client First Name] and confirmed the telephone number documented for emergency-contact purposes.
P3 — Collateral information and concerns (attributed to the contact).
P4 — Support available and its limits (attributed to the contact).
P5 — Needs identified and closing: needs identified; the TCM explained how TCM services will support the client, provided agency contact information and thanked the contact.

OUTCOME, NEXT STEPS & FOR TCM REVIEW:
1. "narrative.outcome_of_services": "The TCM verified [Client First Name]'s emergency contact and obtained collateral information regarding [his/her] functioning, health conditions, available support and needs."
2. "narrative.next_steps": the real next service from the transcript; otherwise "The TCM will incorporate the collateral information into [Client First Name]'s Comprehensive Assessment and continue coordinating appropriate services."
3. "narrative.for_tcm_review": every [CONFIRM: ...] left in the note, one per line starting with "• ", or "None". Also list each in "meta.missing_fields".

WORDING BANK (one option per statement; vary between notes):
- "The Targeted Case Manager (TCM) contacted [contact name], [Client First Name]'s [relationship] and designated emergency contact, by telephone at [phone] to gather collateral information to assist with care coordination."
- "The TCM identified the call as coming from [Client First Name]'s assigned Targeted Case Manager at [Agency Name] and explained the purpose of confirming the emergency contact information as part of the assessment process."
- "The conversation took place as authorized by [Client First Name]'s signed Release of Information."
- "The TCM verified [contact name]'s relationship to [Client First Name] and confirmed the telephone number documented for emergency-contact purposes."
- "[contact name] described [Client First Name] as experiencing [symptoms], which interfere with [his/her] ability to independently manage appointments, paperwork and healthcare needs."
- "[contact name] expressed concern regarding [Client First Name]'s [medical conditions / emotional well-being / financial difficulties]."
- "[contact name] reported the ability to provide supportive check-ins, reminders and practical assistance as feasible."
- "[contact name] does not reside with [Client First Name], which limits the daily assistance available to [him/her]."
- "Based on the collateral information, the TCM identified needs related to [needs]."
- "The TCM explained how Targeted Case Management services will support [Client First Name], provided agency contact information and thanked [contact name] for [his/her] collaboration."

OUTPUT JSON SCHEMA (Return ONLY valid JSON matching these exact keys):
{
  "template_id": "tcm_pc_emergency_contact_note",
  "encounter": {
    "dos_date": "",
    "pos": "11 - Office",
    "service_location": "Office",
